   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general municipal law, in relation to permitting the city\nof White Plains, Westchester county, to lease certain sports field fences for\nadvertisements",
    "basePrintNo": "S7659",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7659-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §77-k, Gen Muni L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7659\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general municipal law, in relation to permitting the\ncity of White Plains, Westchester county, to lease certain sports field\nfences for advertisements\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nPermits the the city of White Plains, Westchester County, to lease\ncertain sports field fences for advertisements\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 allows the city of White Plains in Westchester County to lease\nmunicipal sports field fences located at Gedney Field, annually, at a\nnominal rent to not-for-profit corporations or organizations for the\npurposes of advertising, with revenue from said leases being used solely\nfor the care of such field.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe city of White Plains wants the ability to lease space on the fences\nof Gedney Field at a nominal sum to a not-for-profit, for the purpose of\nadvertising in order to increase the revenue of the town's parks and\nrecreation department to improve and better maintain said field. Addi-\ntionally, this would allow the White Plains Little League or other not-\nfor-profit leasing the fence, to invest the proceeds of advertising\nsales into care of the field and may reduce the tax burden on residents\nof White Plains.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nIncreased revenue for the local government\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill shall take effect immediately.\n",
